    "_postman_id": "0a2f536c-1899-47a7-9a2b-bc5ea302b1f5",
    "name": "📌 Cartesia API",
    "description": "### About Cartesia\n\n\"AI that learns and interacts like humans\"\n\nCartesia builds its own Sonic text-to-speech and Ink speech-to-text models. On the workspace overview it is listed under **Speech & audio**.\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- Postman Account\n    \n- Cartesia Account: [https://cartesia.ai/](https://cartesia.ai/)\n    \n\n### Usage\n\n1. Create a fork\n    \n2. Update collection variables\n    \n3. Send requests\n\nStart with the 🚀 Get Started folder.\n\nAdd your key to your **Postman Vault** as `cartesia_api_key` (Vault icon in the footer, then **Add secret**, using that exact name). Requests read it as `{{vault:cartesia_api_key}}`, so your key never leaves your device.\n\n### Documentation\n\n- API: [https://docs.cartesia.ai/api-reference/tts/bytes](https://docs.cartesia.ai/api-reference/tts/bytes)\n    \n- Models: [https://docs.cartesia.ai/api-reference/stt/transcribe](https://docs.cartesia.ai/api-reference/stt/transcribe)\n\n### Notes\n\nText-to-Speech returns raw audio (WAV). Speech-to-Text needs an audio file selected in the `file` form field.",
